.TH array_find 3
.SH NAME
array_find \- search for an element in an array
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <array.h>

void* \fBarray_find\fP(array* \fIa\fR, uint64 \fImembersize\fR, void* \fIdata\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B array_find
scans the initialized portion of the array pointed to by
.I a
to locate an element that matches the memory block pointed to by
.I data
with size
.I membersize
bytes.

The array is treated as a sequence of elements, each of length
.I membersize.
The comparison is performed using 
.BR byte_equal (3).

.SH RETURN VALUE
.B array_find
returns a pointer to the start of the first element in the array that matches
.I data.
If no such element is found, it returns
.B 0
(NULL).

.SH SEE ALSO
array_indexof(3), array_start(3), array_length(3), byte_equal(3)